{"id": "EUVD-2026-96586", "enisaUuid": "2812939e-001a-3b92-b66e-bb89e984a223", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to create validation rules through the SysCheckRuleController importExcel handler. Attackers can upload a crafted Excel workbook to bypass the system:checkRule:add permission and bulk-create system-wide encoding validation rules with arbitrary regular expression patterns.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:16", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c084_checkrule_import_xlsx.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysCheckRuleController.java#L192-L208", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-checkrule-importexcel"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108647", "GHSA-jqgc-vg5q-wcg4"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "81664fa5-ef01-3ca7-a62a-ee60101a8cf8", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "47c5b180-617e-356f-a963-d36ce8397f24", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}